{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OESA-2026-4917","published":"2026-11-19T01:43:02Z","modified":"2026-11-19T02:00:08.763929404Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-107705"],"summary":"poppler security update","details":"Poppler is a free software utility library for rendering Portable Document Format (PDF) documents. \\ Its development is supported by freedesktop.org. It is commonly used on Linux systems,and is used by \\ the PDF viewers of the open source GNOME and KDE desktop environments.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nPoppler 0.42.0 through 26.10.0 contains a stack-based buffer overflow in Decrypt::revision6Hash() that allows attackers controlling the password to overwrite stack memory when opening AESV3/R6 encrypted PDFs. Attackers can supply a password longer than 127 bytes through applications using the libpoppler, libpoppler-glib or C++ API to overflow the K1 and E buffers, crashing the process or corrupting memory.(CVE-2026-107705)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"poppler","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/poppler&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["poppler-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-cpp-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-cpp-devel-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-debuginfo-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-debugsource-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-devel-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-glib-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-glib-devel-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-qt5-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-qt5-devel-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-qt6-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-qt6-devel-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","poppler-utils-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["poppler-glib-doc-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.noarch.rpm","poppler-help-23.12.0-16.oe2403sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["poppler-23.12.0-16.